# Large raw market-data artifacts are reproducible from fetch.sh; do not commit.
# Patterns are relative to this directory.
*.csv
*.csv.gz
.work/
.work2026/
fetch.log
# ...but the small committed samples must survive the *.csv rule.
!sample/
!sample/*.head.csv
# Phase 5.2 operator MT5 export: the raw UTF-16 source and any large gzip stay
# out; the canonical converted corpus, its sample and metadata are committed.
XAUUSDM1.csv
XAUUSDM1.csv.gz
!xauusd_m1_real.csv
!sample_first_1000.csv
# Phase 5.3: the Dukascopy multi-year corpus is decision-critical (it is the only
# multi-regime window). Commit the deterministic per-year gzip (BID + ASK) so the
# distributed team can consume it; the raw per-minute CSV stays reproducible.
!2021.csv.gz
!2022.csv.gz
!2023.csv.gz
!2024.csv.gz
!2025.csv.gz
# (ask/ is excluded by *.csv / *.csv.gz above; re-include its committed gzip below)
!ask/2021.csv.gz
!ask/2022.csv.gz
!ask/2023.csv.gz
!ask/2024.csv.gz
!ask/2025.csv.gz
